# An allowlist, not a denylist. Excluding target/ and hoping is how a build
# context silently grows: every new top-level directory would have to be
# remembered here, and forgetting one costs a slow build rather than an error.
# Naming the four things the build reads cannot rot that way.
*
!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!src
!LICENSE

# Every entry above is COPYed by the Dockerfile. LICENSE is there because the
# image ships AGPL-3.0-only object code and object code should carry its
# licence; it passes through the build stage only so this repository, rather
# than the checkout's umask, fixes its mode. Nothing is listed here to be
# merely present.
#
# `!src` re-includes the whole subtree on purpose, non-Rust files included.
# src/serve.rs embeds the browser console with include_str! on
# serve/index.html, serve/app.js and serve/style.css, so a rule like
# `src/**/*.html` here would compile-error the build, not slim it.
#
# README.md is out. Cargo.toml declares `readme = "README.md"`, but that field
# is read by `cargo package`, not by the `cargo build` this file runs, and a
# file kept in the context for a consumer that never receives it is the kind of
# thing that reads as correct and is not.
#
# tests/ is out: the image build is not a test gate. `cargo test --release`
# stays the gate, run against a checkout.
